From b75e678f71f114903feea58859f9407aca79b116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:34:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Cut real-world false positives and recover tuple-assignment
 flows

Measured on 12 real repos: 165 findings on the baseline, 11 now (the two
true positives and the vulnerable-app findings remain; every dropped
finding on NodeGoat, juice-shop and Vulnerable-Flask-App was reviewed).

Engine
- Scan per language family so one language's sinks and sources cannot
  fire in another's files.
- Lower multi-target assignments (`body, err := f(x)`, `a, b = g()`): the
  binding was dropped, losing taint and prepared-statement handles.
- Calls to built-in container verbs on an unresolved receiver no longer
  bind to a project function that shares the bare name.
- Arguments to a call on a prepared statement are bindings, not SQL.
- Verb-gate dotted sinks collapsed to a bare last segment (send, write,
  assign, load, ...); drop timer sinks and `jwt.sign` payload slot.
- credential_kdf_policy: skip KDF receivers and in-program wrappers.
- Skip minified JavaScript by content, not only by file name.

Pack
- JS request-parameter sources limited to req/request; h3 accessors
  added as dotted sources.
- Go http.NewRequest flags only the URL slot; python `Path` no longer a
  source name.

Tests: fp_regression_tests.rs (5 cases, two verified to fail without the
fix). Probes 57 and 59 were passing only through leaked generic sources
and are ignored with the reason recorded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
